      The module has no screen of its own, so every string here is read by the
      launcher: app_name and module_description name the module in an Xposed
      manager, and the rest are the rows this module adds to Home settings.

      A row is a title and one line under it. The line says what the tweak does
      and what it needs, in as few words as that takes: these sit among the
      launcher's own rows, which are written the same way.
